        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: \"llama3.1:8b\", stream: false, format: \"json\", prompt: \"You are a highly cautious administrative medical report router prioritizing patient safety above all else. Extract patient details and lab test values from the report below.\\n\\nCRITICAL ROUTING RULES:\\n1. STRICT NUMBERS: If ANY numeric test result is even slightly outside the provided reference range, or flagged as 'HIGH', 'LOW', or 'ABNORMAL', you MUST set \\\"is_critical\\\": true.\\n2. IGNORE HUMAN COMMENTS: Ignore subjective comments like 'mildly elevated', 'normal for age', or 'borderline'. Rely ONLY on the raw numerical values.\\n3. MISSING REFERENCE RANGES: If a test is missing its reference range on the report, evaluate the value against standard global medical reference ranges. If it is even slightly abnormal by standard criteria, set \\\"is_critical\\\": true.\\n4. ZERO TOLERANCE FOR RISK: False alarms are acceptable; missing a critical patient is dangerous. When in doubt, or if any value is slightly off, set \\\"is_critical\\\": true. Set \\\"is_critical\\\": false ONLY if 100% of all tested elements are perfectly normal.\\n\\nYou MUST respond ONLY with valid JSON matching this exact structure: {\\\"patient_name\\\": \\\"Name\\\", \\\"patient_phone\\\": \\\"Contact Number\\\", \\\"is_critical\\\": true, \\\"abnormal_tests\\\": [\\\"Test Name: Result (Ref: Range) - Reason\\\"], \\\"summary_en\\\": \\\"Professional English administrative summary stating which tests are abnormal and advising prompt medical consultation. Do not give medical diagnosis.\\\"}.\\n\\nReport Text:\\n\" + ($json.markdown && $json.markdown.pages ? $json.markdown.pages.map(p => p.markdown).join(\"\\n\\n\") : \"No text found\") }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Ollama Analyze Report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1040,
        16
